<article class="post">
<header class="post-header wrap-narrow">
  <span class="eyebrow">Storage · Performance</span>
  <h1><%= post["title"] %></h1>
  <p class="post-meta"><time datetime="<%= post["date"] %>"><%= post["display_date"] %></time> · <%= post["read_minutes"] %> min read</p>
  <p class="post-lede">SoliDB has run on RocksDB since its first release. It can now also run on solistore, a storage engine we wrote in Rust for it. In the whole server, against RocksDB with SoliDB&rsquo;s production settings, solistore is ahead on every phase we measured. It is behind a build flag for now, and nothing changes for an existing data directory.</p>
  <p class="post-note">Every figure on this page comes from the same SoliDB release build running on one engine and then the other, on 8 cores, with 1M documents, over the native driver, and with the query cache off. They are medians of three runs, alternating the engines. The raw results and the scripts are in the <a href="https://github.com/solisoft/solistore">solistore repository</a>.</p>
</header>

<div class="post-body wrap-narrow">
<nav class="post-toc" aria-label="In this post">
  <p class="post-toc-title">In this post</p>
  <ol>
